<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Allada</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Allada was a kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aja-people">Aja peoples</a> on the coast of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, an early centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>. It was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agaja">King Agaja</a> in the 1720s. The struggle over Allada and neighbouring coastal states drew in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a>, which sought to control trade routes to the coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/allada.jpg" alt="Allada" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fonssagrives, Jean Baptiste Joseph Marie Pascal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roi_d%27Allada-1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
